WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Someone shouts abuse at a woman on a bus.
Someone posts a threat about a mosque.

2
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:20.000
By the time anyone reports it, the post is deleted -
or the video is just a file anyone could have edited.

3
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:35.000
This is Evidence Vault. There's a short walkthrough
the first time you open it - and you can skip it.

4
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Most of what this documents is spoken, not written.
So the main way in is video, with sound.

5
00:00:48.000 --> 00:01:00.000
It's fingerprinted the moment you stop recording,
before it's ever a file that could be edited.

6
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:08.000
That fingerprint is a SHA-256 hash.
Change a single frame and it changes completely.

7
00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:20.000
Only the fingerprint goes to four independent
OpenTimestamps servers, registered on a public blockchain ledger.

8
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:32.000
Your recording never goes anywhere.

9
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:45.000
The recording stays blurred until they choose to look.
Every field is optional.

10
00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:56.000
They choose the category themselves.
We ship no AI classifier.

11
00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:05.000
On-device text recognition in English, Arabic and Urdu,
running in the browser.

12
00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:12.000
Then the part most tools skip.
Where does this actually go?

13
00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:25.000
No police force or court in the US or Canada accepts
evidence through an automated submission.

14
00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:40.000
Most police services have no online hate-crime form.
The NYPD tells you to call your precinct.

15
00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:52.000
For a lawyer or a court, it generates a
certificate of authenticity.

16
00:02:52.000 --> 00:03:00.000
Written to Federal Rules of Evidence 902,
or the Canada Evidence Act.

17
00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:15.000
The export is five files: report, original recording,
proof, certificate, and a plain-text cover letter.

18
00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:25.000
I'm verifying with the official OpenTimestamps client -
not our code.

19
00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:45.000
Anyone can run that check, anywhere, and it keeps working
even if this project disappears tomorrow.

20
00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:52.000
No account. No database. No analytics.
Closing the tab deletes everything.

21
00:03:52.000 --> 00:04:00.000
A timestamp proves when a file existed and that it hasn't
changed - not that its contents are true.
